asr-000512-split-3
00:52:14.040 --> 00:52:28.700
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Mr. President, this representation is honored to sponsor the budget of the Department of Transportation, its attached agencies and corporations. For the record, the recommended new appropriations for the Department of Transportation and its attached agencies is

asr-000513
00:52:28.700 --> 00:53:00.700
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Php 294,568,744,000 plus Php 1,228,338,000 for its attached corporations. With a total budget of Php 295,797,082,000, we are pleased to present some of the key highlights of the Senate Committee Report.

asr-000514
00:53:01.320 --> 00:53:32.900
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: We have restored the funding for the two vital foreign-assisted infrastructure projects to their respective national expenditure program levels. For the Metro Manila Subway project, we restored 19.7 billion covering both the loan proceeds and the government counterpart. Meanwhile, for the North-South Commuter Railway project, we restored 15 billion in loan proceeds. These restorations are crucial to ensuring the timely implementation and completion of these transformative infrastructure projects

asr-000515
00:53:32.900 --> 00:54:01.360
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: honoring our commitments to international development partners and preventing the government from incurring additional commitment fees and other unnecessary financial costs arising from project delays. We have likewise increased the budget for the Active Transport Bike Share System and Safe Pathways Program and the NCR busway to provide our commuting public with safer, more accessible, efficient, and sustainable transportation options.

asr-000516
00:54:02.120 --> 00:54:23.580
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Lastly, we have provided additional funding for the improvement and upgrading of various airports across the country to enhance regional connectivity, [unclear], and economic development and ensure safer, more convenient, and reliable air travel for our Kababayans. Mr. President, we are now ready to answer questions from our colleagues.

